{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<h1>Tables</h1>
<p class="hint">Somewhere for a dynamic page to keep things. Each table you make becomes a small set
  of JavaScript functions &mdash; the only way a page can ask it anything, so every query is one
  somebody wrote down.</p>

{{#unavailable}}<p class="problem">This community's data file could not be opened, so there are no
  tables. The site is serving normally; only this is affected.</p>{{/unavailable}}

{{^unavailable}}
<div class="doing"><a class="btn" href="{{newUrl}}">New table</a></div>

{{^any}}<p class="hint">No tables yet.</p>{{/any}}
{{#any}}
<p class="count">{{count}} table(s), in <code>{{file}}</code></p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>table</th><th>fields</th><th>indexed</th><th>rows</th><th>what a page can call</th><th></th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{{#tables}}<tr>
    <td class="mono"><a href="{{editUrl}}">{{name}}</a></td>
    <td class="dim">{{fields}}</td>
    <td class="dim mono">{{#anyIndexes}}{{indexes}}{{/anyIndexes}}{{^anyIndexes}}&mdash;{{/anyIndexes}}</td>
    <td class="dim mono">{{rows}}</td>
    <td class="dim mono">{{#functions}}<div>{{.}}</div>{{/functions}}</td>
    <td class="actions"><a href="{{editUrl}}">edit</a></td>
  </tr>{{/tables}}</tbody>
</table>
{{/any}}

<h2>Reading one from a page</h2>
<pre><code>var rows = signups_list_job('bread');
rows.forEach(function (r) { render('&lt;li&gt;' + r.who + '&lt;/li&gt;'); });</code></pre>
<p class="hint">Every row arrives with its <code>id</code> and the fields you declared, typed the way
  you declared them. A page reads; it never writes &mdash; a dynamic page runs for every request
  including a crawler's, and a page that could insert would be a table filling itself with whatever
  fetched it.</p>
<p class="hint">These tables live in a file of their own beside the accounts database, so nothing
  you do here can reshape the community's own tables.</p>
{{/unavailable}}
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
